}
```

The check at line 134 is in the innermost else branch. If `name[i]` is printable ASCII (the first if branch), only `name[i]` is accessed, which is within bounds. If `name[i]` is not printable and `name[i] < 10` (the second if branch), only `name[i]` is accessed. If `name[i]` is not printable and `name[i] >= 10` (the final else branch), `name[i]` and `name[i + 1]` are accessed, but the check at line 134 prevents reading past the buffer.

So `get_unicode_name` seems safe.

